\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Experimental design and comparison units. (a) Four contact-derived graphs provide seven admitted combinations of network and seed budget; filled circles indicate inclusion and the cross marks the SFHH setting excluded during resource preflight. (b) Each setting is crossed with two random-world paths and three nested selection budgets, giving 42 conditions. (c) Each condition runs full greedy and three degree-pool arms, giving 168 arm executions. Eligibility alone changes between arms; the diffusion topology is shared. The small networks illustrate this distinction and do not encode measured pool sizes. (d) Selected sets are evaluated on 2,000 worlds disjoint from selection and shared across arms, selection budgets and seed budgets within each pair of network and path. Seed traces and timing come from selection records and the timed execution; spread comes from evaluation. Diagram tiles are schematic. Conditions sharing data or worlds are dependent comparisons, not independent network replicates.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:2}{{2}{7}{Experimental design and comparison units. (a) Four contact-derived graphs provide seven admitted combinations of network and seed budget; filled circles indicate inclusion and the cross marks the SFHH setting excluded during resource preflight. (b) Each setting is crossed with two random-world paths and three nested selection budgets, giving 42 conditions. (c) Each condition runs full greedy and three degree-pool arms, giving 168 arm executions. Eligibility alone changes between arms; the diffusion topology is shared. The small networks illustrate this distinction and do not encode measured pool sizes. (d) Selected sets are evaluated on 2,000 worlds disjoint from selection and shared across arms, selection budgets and seed budgets within each pair of network and path. Seed traces and timing come from selection records and the timed execution; spread comes from evaluation. Diagram tiles are schematic. Conditions sharing data or worlds are dependent comparisons, not independent network replicates}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Historical graph instances used by the frozen confirmation run. Edge counts include both directions of each aggregated contact link. Conditions count world-path and selection-budget combinations, not independent datasets.}}{7}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:2}{{2}{7}{Historical graph instances used by the frozen confirmation run. Edge counts include both directions of each aggregated contact link. Conditions count world-path and selection-budget combinations, not independent datasets}{table.2}{}}
