\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Fewer pooled ties coexist with changes in final seed sets. (a) The proportion of greedy rounds with multiple best-scoring candidates at each selection budget; labels show percentages and counts. Each denominator is 160 rounds from eight traces of length five and six of length 20, so longer traces contribute more weight. (b) Counts of blocks whose final unordered full-greedy seed set changes at each adjacent budget transition, computed post-hoc from frozen outputs. These descriptive counts use dependent rounds and repeated network instances; no inferential intervals or significance tests are shown. The panels do not establish utility loss or a causal relationship between ties and set changes. Individual tie trajectories appear in Fig. 4, and final-set overlaps in Fig. 7.}}{10}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:3}{{3}{10}{Fewer pooled ties coexist with changes in final seed sets. (a) The proportion of greedy rounds with multiple best-scoring candidates at each selection budget; labels show percentages and counts. Each denominator is 160 rounds from eight traces of length five and six of length 20, so longer traces contribute more weight. (b) Counts of blocks whose final unordered full-greedy seed set changes at each adjacent budget transition, computed post-hoc from frozen outputs. These descriptive counts use dependent rounds and repeated network instances; no inferential intervals or significance tests are shown. The panels do not establish utility loss or a causal relationship between ties and set changes. Individual tie trajectories appear in Fig. 4, and final-set overlaps in Fig. 7}{figure.3}{}}
